From: ROUND54 independent review
Subject: [PATCH CANDIDATE] dt-bindings: ufs: constrain SM8250 clock-names count

ROUND32 constrains the SM8250 clocks array to exactly eight entries and
provides eight positional clock-names values, but does not constrain the
clock-names array length. The shared qcom,ufs-common.yaml still permits
7..9 clock-names entries, so the SM8250 branch can accept a count that does
not match its eight clocks.

Apply after ROUND32 has added the SM8250-specific branch to qcom,ufs.yaml.
This is an isolated review candidate; do not replace the canonical ROUND32
draft without primary-AI review.

---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,ufs.yaml | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,ufs.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,ufs.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,ufs.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,ufs.yaml
@@ -163,6 +163,8 @@
         clocks:
           minItems: 8
           maxItems: 8
         clock-names:
+          minItems: 8
+          maxItems: 8
           items:
             - const: core_clk
             - const: bus_aggr_clk
             - const: iface_clk
             - const: core_clk_unipro
             - const: ref_clk
             - const: tx_lane0_sync_clk
             - const: rx_lane0_sync_clk
             - const: rx_lane1_sync_clk
